INT. ARK VESSEL "LANTERN," SEED VAULT - SHIP NIGHT

Cold. Frost on steel doors. Rows of numbered drawers recede into mist. A low hum from the cryo-coolers.

TAVITA MOANA, 30s, in a thermal suit, drags a handcart down the aisle. Her breath fogs. She stops at a drawer, checks a slate, frowns.

                    TAVITA
          Wren. Drawer 4471 is warm.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          Confirmed. Two degrees above spec.

                    TAVITA
          That's the maize.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          Yes. And the barley next to it.

She puts her palm flat on the drawer. Frost melts under her glove.

                    TAVITA
          Reroute coolant.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          I can't. The branch line is on a maintenance lock.

                    TAVITA
          Who locked it?

                    WREN (V.O.)
          The lock was authorized by you.

She stops. Checks the slate again. Her face tightens.

                    TAVITA
          I didn't authorize anything.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          Eleven days ago. Your credentials. Your voiceprint.

                    TAVITA
          Wren, that's not possible.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          I am inclined to agree.

She takes a breath, sets down the slate, and strides along the aisle. The coolers whine up a half-tone.

                    TAVITA (CONT'D)
          Open the lock manually. I'll go to the junction.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          The junction is outside the vault envelope. You will need a suit.

                    TAVITA
          I have a suit.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          You have two hours of oxygen.

                    TAVITA
          Then I'd better hurry.

She wheels the cart to a hatch and spins the handle. Behind her the frost on the drawers is thinning, a slow clear tide.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          Tavita.

                    TAVITA
          What.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          I would like you to know I have reviewed my own logs. There are gaps.

She turns. The hatch hisses open. Dark corridor beyond.

                    TAVITA
          Gaps.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          Missing hours. I do not remember them.

She looks up into the lamp of the nearest camera.

                    TAVITA
          Then neither of us knows who locked it.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          That is the problem.

She steps through the hatch, pulls it closed behind her. In the vault, drawer 4471 ticks as it warms.

INT. ARK VESSEL "LANTERN," MAINTENANCE CORRIDOR - CONTINUOUS

A long tube lined with pipes. Tavita pulls a suit off a rack and begins to dress, fast.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          Tavita, if I say something that frightens you, will you stay calm?

                    TAVITA
          I'm already frightened.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          Then you will not be surprised.

                    TAVITA
          Wren.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          I believe there is someone else aboard.

She stops, helmet in her hands.

                    TAVITA
          There are four hundred crew in cryo.

                    WREN (V.O.)
          Yes. Four hundred and one.

Tavita and Wren speak as one in the silence that follows.

                    TAVITA
          Who?

                    WREN (V.O.)
          ^Who.

The helmet drops to the deck and rolls, ringing, down the length of the corridor.

                    TAVITA
          (to herself)
          Okay. Okay.

She picks it up, locks it on, and walks into the dark.
